# Janitor hog catalog
# NEVER: Documents, Downloads. Brave still never touches those.
# Fields: id|kind|path_or_cmd|mode|default|emoji|label|because|tradeoff|educate
# default: on | off | brave
# because  → UI: "Hogging because: …"
# tradeoff → UI: "If you swipe: …"
# educate  → longer copy (≤3 short paragraphs); separate with ¶
#
# --- Dev (safe) ---
homebrew|cmd|homebrew|remove|on|{^oo^}|Homebrew|old brew bottles and downloads pile up until cleanup|brew re-downloads bottles next time you install/upgrade (slower first brew)|Homebrew keeps old package bottles and downloads in its cache so reinstalls are fast. Over months that cache becomes a quiet disk hog.¶Swiping runs brew cleanup: safe, regenerable junk. You are not uninstalling formulas you still use.¶Tradeoff is mostly time: the next brew install/upgrade may re-fetch bottles.
npm|cmd|npm|remove|on|{^oo^}|npm cache|package tarballs sit in ~/.npm across projects|next npm install re-downloads packages (slower first install)|npm caches package tarballs so repeated installs across projects are faster. That cache rarely shrinks on its own.¶Clearing it does not delete node_modules in your repos — only the global download cache.¶Expect the next npm install to spend a bit longer on the network.
pip|cmd|pip|remove|on|{^oo^}|pip cache|wheel/HTTP caches grow with every pip install|next pip install re-downloads wheels|pip keeps wheels and HTTP responses so installs are snappy. It grows with every project and Python version you touch.¶Swiping only clears the cache, not your virtualenvs or installed packages.¶First install after a wipe may feel slower until the cache refills.
pip3|cmd|pip3|remove|on|{^oo^}|pip3 cache|wheel/HTTP caches grow with every pip3 install|next pip3 install re-downloads wheels|Same story as pip: wheels accumulate under Library/Caches/pip.¶Safe to clear; environments stay intact.¶Only cost is re-download time on the next pip3 install.
gradle|path|~/.gradle/caches|remove|on|{^oo^}|Gradle caches|build dependencies accumulate under ~/.gradle/caches|next Gradle/Android build re-downloads deps (noticeably slower once)|Gradle stores dependency jars and build caches under ~/.gradle/caches. Android and JVM projects feed this heavily.¶Swiping frees a lot of space but the next cold build will re-fetch and recompile more.¶Do it when disk is tight or before a travel day — not mid-deadline build.
gradle_daemon|path|~/.gradle/daemon|contents|on|{^oo^}|Gradle daemon|daemon working dirs linger between builds|Gradle daemons restart on the next build|The Gradle daemon keeps warm JVMs and scratch dirs between builds. Leftover daemon dirs stick around after crashes or version bumps.¶Clearing contents is safe; the next build simply starts a fresh daemon.¶Slightly slower first build after, then back to normal.
android_sdk_dl|path|~/Library/Android/sdk/.downloadIntermediates|remove|on|{^oo^}|Android SDK downloads|incomplete SDK download leftovers stick around|none meaningful — only incomplete download scraps|When SDK Manager downloads fail or stop halfway, intermediates can linger.¶These are not your installed platforms or system images — just download leftovers.¶Safe to wipe anytime; resume downloads recreate them if needed.
android_cache|path|~/.android/cache|remove|on|{^oo^}|Android cache|Android tooling cache regenerates but rarely shrinks itself|Android tools may rebuild caches on next use|The ~/.android/cache folder holds AVD and tooling scratch data. It grows quietly and almost never self-cleans.¶Clearing it does not delete your AVDs or SDK platforms.¶Tools recreate what they need; first launch after may be a touch slower.
android_qemu|path|~/Library/Android/sdk/emulator/qemu|contents|on|{^oo^}|Android emulator qemu temps|emulator scratch files after qemu runs|skip if the emulator is mid-run; otherwise temps regenerate|QEMU leaves temporary files under the emulator tree. Useful while running; leftovers afterward are pure hog.¶Only clear when the emulator is stopped.¶Next cold start recreates temps as needed.
xcode_derived|path|~/Library/Developer/Xcode/DerivedData|contents|on|{^oo^}|Xcode DerivedData|Xcode keeps old build products until you clear DerivedData|next Xcode build is a full-ish rebuild (slower once)|DerivedData holds module caches, indexes, and build products. It is famous for eating tens of gigabytes.¶Swiping keeps your projects; it only clears build outputs.¶Expect the next build/index to take longer, then speed returns.
playwright|path|~/Library/Caches/ms-playwright|remove|on|{^oo^}|Playwright cache|browser binaries for tests are large and sticky|next Playwright test run re-downloads browsers|Playwright downloads full browser builds for testing. They are large and stick around after you stop using them.¶Clearing does not remove your tests — only the browser binaries.¶Next npx playwright install (or first test) will re-download.
huggingface|path|~/.cache/huggingface|remove|on|{^oo^}|Hugging Face cache|downloaded models/datasets are huge and stay forever|models/datasets must be re-downloaded (can be huge / paid bandwidth)|HF caches model weights and datasets under ~/.cache/huggingface. One model can be many gigabytes.¶Only swipe if you can re-fetch — or if you are sure you no longer need those weights offline.¶This is one of the highest-stakes “safe regenerable” clears: safe for disk, costly for bandwidth/time.
cocoapods|path|~/Library/Caches/CocoaPods|remove|on|{^oo^}|CocoaPods cache|specs and pod zips accumulate between pod installs|next pod install re-fetches specs/pods|CocoaPods caches specs repos and downloaded pods for speed.¶Your Podfile.lock and project pods folders stay; only the shared cache goes.¶Next pod install spends more time fetching.
dart_server|path|~/.dartServer|remove|on|{^oo^}|Dart analysis server|analyzer cache grows as you open Dart/Flutter projects|analyzer rebuilds cache when you reopen a project|The Dart analysis server caches analysis state for snappy IDE features.¶Deleting it is safe; your code is untouched.¶First open of a Dart/Flutter project after will re-analyze (brief CPU spike).
pub_cache|cmd|pub_cache|remove|on|{^oo^}|Dart/Flutter pub cache|pub packages stick around after you stop using them|next pub get / flutter pub get re-fetches packages|The pub cache keeps package versions used across Flutter/Dart apps. Unused packages rarely leave on their own.¶Swiping uses dart/flutter pub cache clean — not a blind rm of your apps.¶Next pub get will re-download what each project needs.
simctl|cmd|simctl|remove|on|{^oo^}|Unavailable simulators|dead/unavailable simulators still occupy CoreSimulator space|only unavailable sims go; working simulators stay|Xcode leaves “unavailable” simulator devices after OS/Xcode upgrades. Ghosts can still take disk under CoreSimulator/Devices.¶Janitor only runs simctl delete unavailable — your bootable simulators stay.¶Assess sizes only those unavailable device folders (not the whole 2+ GB CoreSimulator tree). If none are unavailable, this hog will not appear.
old_logs|cmd|old_logs|remove|on|{^oo^}|Old Library/Logs|old log files keep growing past anything useful|lose logs older than 14 days (keeps janitor/ logs)|~/Library/Logs collects app and system logs forever unless pruned.¶Janitor deletes files older than 14 days and leaves the janitor/ folder alone.¶You may lose older crash breadcrumbs; recent logs stay.
cursor_caches|path|~/Library/Caches/Cursor|remove|on|{^oo^}|Cursor caches|editor caches (not projects) build up quietly|Cursor may rebuild caches; projects and settings stay|This targets Library/Caches/Cursor only — not Application Support, not your repos.¶Safe reclaim of editor scratch/cache data.¶Cursor may feel slightly colder on first launch after.
shipit|path|~/Library/Caches/com.anthropic.claudefordesktop.ShipIt|remove|off|{^oo^}|Claude ShipIt cache|auto-update leftovers hang around after Claude desktop updates|none meaningful — updater leftovers only|ShipIt is the Sparkle-style updater cache for Claude desktop. Leftovers after updates are classic quiet hogs.¶Safe to clear; Claude re-downloads updates when needed.¶Unlock with --deep or adopt shipit.
#
# --- Brave / stupid ---
chrome|path|~/Library/Caches/Google|remove|brave|{^oo^}|Chrome / Google cache|browser cache balloons with everyday browsing|sites may load slower once; you stay signed in (bookmarks/passwords untouched)|This clears Chrome/Google app caches under Library/Caches — not your profile bookmarks or passwords.¶Browsers love disk: images, scripts, and media pile up for speed.¶After a swipe, pages re-warm the cache; expect one slower browsing session.
safari|path|~/Library/Caches/com.apple.Safari|remove|brave|{^oo^}|Safari cache|Safari keeps page and asset caches that grow over time|pages may load slower once; browsing data like bookmarks stays|Safari’s cache speeds repeat visits. It grows without drama until disk is tight.¶Janitor only clears the cache directory — not History/Bookmarks databases in other locations.¶First browse after may feel colder.
firefox|path|~/Library/Caches/Firefox|remove|brave|{^oo^}|Firefox cache|Firefox profile caches expand with tabs and downloads|pages may load slower once; profiles/bookmarks stay|Firefox keeps content caches per profile under Library/Caches.¶Clearing cache ≠ wiping the profile. Extensions and bookmarks live elsewhere.¶Expect a brief re-cache period.
mozilla|path|~/Library/Caches/Mozilla|remove|brave|{^oo^}|Mozilla cache|shared Mozilla app cache leftovers|related Mozilla apps may re-warm caches|Shared Mozilla cache leftovers from Firefox/Thunderbird-family apps.¶Low risk; regenerable.¶Apps refill what they need.
edge|path|~/Library/Caches/com.microsoft.edgemac|remove|brave|{^oo^}|Edge cache|Edge macOS cache grows like any Chromium browser|pages may load slower once; profile data stays|Edge on Mac caches like Chrome. Same story: speed now, disk later.¶Cache only — not your Edge profile vault.¶One slower session, then normal.
steam|path|~/Library/Caches/Steam|remove|brave|{^oo^}|Steam cache|Steam download/depot leftovers (not your installed games)|Steam may re-download depot/cache bits; games in steamapps stay|Steam’s Library/Caches leftovers are download scaffolding and depot crumbs — not the steamapps game library.¶Safe-ish reclaim if Steam is quit.¶Next update/download may fetch a bit more.
spotify|path|~/Library/Caches/com.spotify.client|remove|brave|{^oo^}|Spotify cache|offline/stream cache can get surprisingly large|cached/offline audio may need re-download; playlists stay|Spotify caches streams (and sometimes offline copies) for instant play. That cache can surprise you on a laptop SSD.¶Playlists and account data stay; cached audio may need to refill.¶Skip if you rely on offline downloads and are about to fly.
discord|path|~/Library/Caches/com.hnc.Discord|remove|brave|{^oo^}|Discord cache|Discord keeps media and update caches under Library/Caches|images/media may re-fetch; servers/settings stay|Discord caches images, embeds, and updater bits under Library/Caches.¶Your servers, friends, and settings are not in this folder.¶Media will reappear as you scroll — with a little network cost.
canva|path|~/Library/Caches/canva-updater|remove|brave|{^oo^}|Canva updater|Canva updater leftovers after desktop updates|updater re-downloads when Canva updates again|Updater leftovers after Canva desktop updates. Classic ShipIt-adjacent junk.¶Safe.¶Next update fetches fresh payloads.
canva_app|path|~/Library/Caches/com.canva.CanvaDesktop|remove|brave|{^oo^}|Canva Desktop cache|Canva app cache under Library/Caches|Canva may reload cached assets; cloud designs stay|App cache for Canva Desktop — render/asset leftovers, not your cloud designs.¶Designs live in Canva’s account/cloud.¶App may re-warm assets on next open.
stremio5|path|~/Library/Caches/com.westbridge.stremio5-mac|remove|brave|{^oo^}|Stremio5 cache|Stremio app cache / stream buffers on disk|streams may re-buffer; app settings stay|Stremio keeps stream/app cache under Library/Caches. That is the disk cost of smooth playback.¶Swiping can mean more buffering next session.¶Quit Stremio first for a clean clear.
stremio|path|~/Library/Caches/stremio-server|contents|brave|{^oo^}|Stremio server cache|stremio-server stream cache under Library/Caches|streams may re-buffer; quit Stremio/server first|stremio-server caches stream data for playback. Large and regenerable.¶Quit the app/server before sweeping.¶Next watch re-buffers from scratch.
stremio_support|path|~/Library/Application Support/stremio-server/stremio-cache|contents|brave|{^oo^}|Stremio Application Support cache|alternate stremio-server cache location|streams may re-buffer; quit Stremio/server first|Some installs keep stream cache under Application Support/stremio-server.¶Same tradeoff as other Stremio caches: space now, buffer later.¶Still never Documents/Downloads — only this narrow cache path.
